.TH RUSTFETCH 1 "September 2026" "rustfetch 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rustfetch, rfetch \- blazing-fast, memory-safe system information fetch tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rustfetch
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B rfetch
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBRustFetch\fR is a lightweight, ultra-fast system information tool written in pure Rust.
Designed as a memory-safe, zero-fork alternative to Neofetch and Fastfetch, it gathers
system telemetry directly from Linux kernel interfaces (\fB/proc\fR and \fB/sys\fR) without
spawning shell sub-processes.
.PP
The executable is also available under the alias \fBrfetch\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-preset " \fINAME\fR"
Apply a built-in layout and formatting preset. Available presets:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
\fBdefault\fR: Standard clean view with auto-detected distro ASCII logo.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcard\fR: Rounded border card container with centered ASCII art.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBminimal\fR: Compact hardware view without ASCII art or icons.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBmodern\fR: Dot separator with colorful section banners.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcompact\fR: Terse key-value layout with short labels.
.RE
.TP
.BR \-\-benchmark
Run execution profiler measuring microsecond-level latency per telemetry module.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " \fIPATH\fR"
Path to custom TOML configuration file (defaults to \fI~/.config/rustfetch/config.toml\fR).
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-image " \fIPATH\fR"
Render an image instead of ASCII art using the Kitty Graphics Protocol.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-logo " \fINAME\fR"
Override ASCII logo (e.g., \fIarch\fR, \fIubuntu\fR, \fIfedora\fR, \fIdebian\fR, \fIvoid\fR, \fIalpine\fR, \fInixos\fR, \fIgentoo\fR, etc.).
.TP
.BR \-\-color " \fICOLOR\fR"
Override primary theme color (e.g., \fIcyan\fR, \fIblue\fR, \fIgreen\fR, \fIred\fR, \fIyellow\fR, \fImagenta\fR, \fIwhite\fR, or hex \fI#33aadd\fR).
.TP
.BR \-\-align " \fIALIGN\fR"
Set layout alignment: \fIleft\fR, \fIright\fR, or \fIcenter\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-center
Shortcut to horizontally center both logo and system information in terminal.
.TP
.BR \-\-json
Output system information in structured JSON format.
.TP
.BR \-\-live
Run in continuous real-time monitor mode with live metrics update.
.TP
.BR \-\-dump\-config
Print current active configuration to stdout.
.TP
.BR \-\-generate\-config
Generate default \fIconfig.toml\fR file in \fI~/.config/rustfetch/\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-import\-fastfetch
Import existing Fastfetch configuration and convert it into RustFetch TOML format.
.TP
.BR \-\-completions " \fISHELL\fR"
Generate shell auto-completion script for \fIbash\fR, \fIzsh\fR, or \fIfish\fR.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help information.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version information.
.SH MODULES
RustFetch supports the following modular telemetry collectors:
.TP
.B os
Operating system name, distribution ID, and release from \fI/etc/os-release\fR.
.TP
.B kernel
Running Linux kernel release from \fBuname(2)\fR.
.TP
.B uptime
System uptime parsed from \fI/proc/uptime\fR.
.TP
.B packages
Total installed package count across pacman, dpkg, rpm, flatpak, apk, xbps, nix, emerge, and snap.
.TP
.B shell
Active user shell and version from \fB$SHELL\fR.
.TP
.B display
Connected monitors, active resolutions, and refresh rates (parsed via EDID from \fI/sys/class/drm\fR).
.TP
.B de
Desktop Environment (\fB$XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP\fR or \fB$DESKTOP_SESSION\fR).
.TP
.B wm
Window Manager (Wayland compositor or X11 WM detection).
.TP
.B terminal
Terminal emulator name detected via parent process inspection.
.TP
.B cpu
Processor model name, core/thread count, and maximum frequency from \fI/proc/cpuinfo\fR.
.TP
.B gpu
Graphics cards detected via PCI class inspection in \fI/sys/bus/pci/devices\fR.
.TP
.B memory
RAM usage and total capacity parsed directly from \fI/proc/meminfo\fR.
.TP
.B swap
Swap space usage parsed from \fI/proc/meminfo\fR.
.TP
.B disk
Root and mounted filesystem usage.
.TP
.B battery
Battery status and charge percentage from \fI/sys/class/power_supply\fR.
.TP
.B sound
Default audio sink volume and mute status via WirePlumber / PulseAudio.
.TP
.B wifi
Active wireless interface SSID and signal quality percentage.
.TP
.B processes
Total running process count and 1-minute load average from \fI/proc/loadavg\fR.
.TP
.B media
Current MPRIS player status and playback title (optional, disabled by default).
.TP
.B colors
Terminal 8-color palette preview bar.
.TP
.B custom
Arbitrary user-defined text line.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
If set to any non-empty value (regardless of content), ANSI color codes are completely disabled.
.TP
.B TERM
When set to \fIdumb\fR, ANSI formatting is stripped. When set to \fIlinux\fR (Linux virtual console/TTY), TrueColor hex codes are automatically mapped to 16 standard ANSI colors for maximum readability.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/rustfetch/config.toml
Main user configuration file.
.TP
.I ~/.config/rustfetch/logos/
Directory for custom ASCII logo files.
